        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45960703?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Google Chrome deprecated (Browsing) Topics API.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Google Chrome deprecated (Browsing) Topics API, so mark the following MDN features deprecated:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>document.browsingTopics()</li>\n<li>browsingtopics attribute on HTML &lt;iframe&gt;</li>\n<li>browsingTopics option in fetch()</li>\n<li>Sec-Browsing-Topics HTTP request header</li>\n<li>Observe-Browsing-Topics HTTP response header</li>\n<li>HTTP header Permissions-Policy directive browsing-topics</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Source:<br>\n<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/_R85yctz4Rs\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/_R85yctz4Rs</a></p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tracking MDN issue <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3603007045\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28417\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28417/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28417\">#28417</a>.</p>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28418",
            "title": "Deprecate Google Privacy Sandbox (Browsing) Topics API",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-18T10:41:41.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-08T12:53:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "bershanskiy",
                "url": "https://github.com/bershanskiy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Unmarks Firefox as partial for <code class=\"notranslate\">::highlight</code> CSS Selector, and splits up the existing notes, adding bug links.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I challenge the following <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/tree/main/docs/data-guidelines#partial_implementation-general-usage-guidelines\">requirement for partial implementation</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The browser's support has a demonstrable negative impact on web developers.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3586286163\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28374\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28374/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28374\">#28374</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28375",
            "title": "Unmark Firefox as partial for `::highlight` CSS selector",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-09T14:46:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-04T12:12:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chromium browsers support <a href=\"https://privacysandbox.google.com/protections/user-agent\" rel=\"nofollow\">User-Agent reduction</a>, which means that features such as the <code class=\"notranslate\">User-Agent</code> HTTP header provide less-specific information in an effort to reduce their effectiveness for fingerprinting/tracking.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds data points covering User-Agent reduction to relevant web platform features that I know to be affected by the change.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Compat data sources:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>From looking at <a href=\"https://blog.chromium.org/2021/09/user-agent-reduction-origin-trial-and-dates.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://blog.chromium.org/2021/09/user-agent-reduction-origin-trial-and-dates.html</a>, it looks like rollout of UA reduction to 100% of Chromium desktop users occurred in version 110, while the version was 113 for Chromium Android users. I asked <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/miketaylr/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/miketaylr\">@miketaylr</a> about this, and he confirmed it to be correct.</li>\n<li>From looking at <a href=\"https://www.chromium.org/updates/ua-reduction/#applicable-platforms\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.chromium.org/updates/ua-reduction/#applicable-platforms</a>, it looks like Android WebView should be <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Another question for Mike: For all of these data points, I used <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/ua-client-hints/#user-agent\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wicg.github.io/ua-client-hints/#user-agent</a> as the <code class=\"notranslate\">spec_url</code>. Are there better spec URLs we can point to for these individual features?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR is part of the final set of privacy sandbox information to be added to MDN. Much of it is being removed, but this feature is stable and will be kept, so it should be added.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28275",
            "title": "Chrome 110 applies User-Agent reduction to Navigator properties + `User-Agent` header",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-07T14:33:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-23T15:21:08.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Extracts HTML <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;datalist&gt;</code> input type subfeatures, and duplicates these below <code class=\"notranslate\">html.input.elements.type_*</code>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To review, look at \"grouped by change\" in <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28189#issuecomment-3401538971\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28189/hovercard\">this comment</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Once landed, we can tackle the issues mentioned in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2801257212\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25723\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25723/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25723\">#25723</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28189",
            "title": "Extract HTML `<datalist>` input type subfeatures",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-13T15:14:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T12:23:54.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43868318?u=3f179cacfd70db40ae7c11f1b951533a8ebf45bf&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Added caret.json with compatibility data structure</li>\n<li>Currently no browser support, but Chrome support expected soon</li>\n<li>Marked as experimental and standard track</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27904",
            "title": "Add CSS caret property (WIP - awaiting browser support)",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-16T16:55:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-16T16:54:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "yashrajbharti",
                "url": "https://github.com/yashrajbharti"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/644927?u=790461985bc61a38ef27bed89be1fdec9ace7cbc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari 14.1 and newer displays a time picker for <code class=\"notranslate\">datetime-local</code>.<br>\n<code class=\"notranslate\">datetime-local</code> was not working correctly in one of the Safari tech previews but was fixed before the final 14.1 release.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See the Safari 14.1 release note (<a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-14_1-release-notes\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-14_1-release-notes</a>)</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Added support for HTML date, time, and datetime-local input types in macOS, enabling date and time controls in forms.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is confirmed by the according issue (comment 27): <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">More confirmations:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>With screenshot: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"717735603\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/issues/5646\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5646/hovercard?comment_id=715180664&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5646#issuecomment-715180664\">Fyrd/caniuse#5646 (comment)</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"728444766\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/issues/5669\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5669/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/pull/5669\">Fyrd/caniuse#5669</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A jsfiddle to test yourself: <a href=\"https://jsfiddle.net/8gw2yk5e/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://jsfiddle.net/8gw2yk5e/</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=214946#c27</a> (see comment 27)</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27762",
            "title": "Remove note about Safari time picker for `datetime-local`",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-05T15:34:55.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-05T09:18:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "mkurz",
                "url": "https://github.com/mkurz"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is a bit of a test PR to see if we could add spec_urls everywhere (especially for behavioral sub features).<br>\nSome things came up where we should probably agree on spec_url consistency for a few common sub features:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>worker_support</li>\n<li>iterable sub features (forEach, keys, values, iterator, etc)</li>\n<li>secure_context_required<br>\nI decided to use the spec_url for the interface itself, happy to hear other thoughts.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, I think when a sub aspect of e.g. a method is described then it is okay to link to the same spec section as the method. So, basically the sub feature gets the same spec_url as the parent feature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I marked standard_track false for a few things: CSSPrimitiveValue, CSSValue, CSSValueList, DOMError, FeaturePolicy. Doesn't look like these will be going anywhere.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #27456.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3279237470\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27456\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27456/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27456\">#27456</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27671",
            "title": "Add more spec_urls; set some standard_tracks to false (APIs A-E)",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-29T11:30:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-26T13:10:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        }
    ]
